+---
+id: task-002-rental-availability-query
+type: task
+title: "Rental availability query"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Rental availability query
+
+## Request
+
+The desk needs to see at a glance what can still be rented. Add `availability(query)` to the rental
+service from task-001, where `query` is `{ start, end, kind }` and `kind` is optional. It returns the ids
+of the equipment of that kind, or of any kind when `kind` is not given, that is free for the whole period,
+sorted.
+
+## Choices made for this request
+
+- The period (`start`, `end`) is validated exactly as `quote` and `book` validate it: whole UTC days, not
+  empty or reversed, valid ISO-8601 UTC. An invalid period throws.
+- An unknown `kind` (anything other than `'board'` or `'sail'`) throws. An omitted or `undefined` `kind`
+  means any kind.
+- "Free" means no existing booking overlaps the period, using the same overlap rule as `book`, so
+  back-to-back periods do not conflict.
+- Ids are sorted with the default string order (`Array.prototype.sort()`).
+- When nothing is free, the result is an empty array; this is not an error.
+- `availability` does not reserve anything.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC9: `availability` is a method of the service returned by `createRentalService()`.
+- AC10: With no `kind`, it returns the ids of all registered equipment that are free for the whole period,
+  sorted.
+- AC11: With `kind`, it returns only the ids of equipment of that kind that are free, sorted.
+- AC12: An item booked for a period overlapping the query is excluded; an item whose booking ends where the
+  query starts (or starts where it ends) is included.
+- AC13: `availability` throws for an invalid period (same rules as AC4) and for an unknown `kind`.
+- AC14: Returns an empty array when no equipment is free, and does not change any booking.
+
+## School rules (apply)
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents (not involved here).
+2. Times are UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+3. A booking covers whole days: start and end are at midnight UTC.
+4. The same item cannot be booked for overlapping periods.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Feature: rental module (booking desk). Story: the desk sees what can still be rented.
+Requirements: school rules 2–4 above; extends task-001 (AC1–AC8). Tests cover AC9–AC14 with happy and
+error paths.
